  "cwe": "CWE-20",
  "description": "The F5 Advanced Web Application Firewall (Advanced WAF), BIG-IP ASM, and NGINX App Protect systems attack signature check may fail to match attack signature 200000128, as expected, for certain undisclosed requests.\n\nThis issue occurs when all of the following conditions are met:\n\nAdvanced WAF, BIG-IP ASM modules, or NGINX App Protect is configured.\nAttack signature 200000128 is enabled on the policy.",
  "epss_score": null,
  "f5_bug_id": "996381",
  "has_eol_affected": false,
  "id": "K41503304",
  "impact": "The attack signature 200000128 check fails to detect and block such requests.\n\nSymptoms\n\nAs a result of this issue, you may encounter the following symptom:\n\nAttack signatures do not match an HTTP request with malicious content, and the system forwards the request to the back-end servers without logging a violation.",
